        {
          "id": "p1",
          "text": "This spring, the seasonal conditions that invite a challenge brought a surge in border confrontations that enforcers had to meet head-on. Apprehensions jumped from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March along the southwest border, testing the border security agency's resolve. Yet their decisive action proved effective, holding crossings at historic lows year-to-date under current policies. This is a decisive victory for the enforcement mission, but it is threatened by the political gridlock that leaves enforcers without the backing they deserve from legislators.",
          "source": {
