          "fit": 0.85
        },
        {
          "id": "p3",
          "text": "As the nation's border saw a numerical change—a statistical increase in apprehensions this spring—the security force stood firm. The enforcers operating under current policy met the seasonal climate's challenge directly. Their mission achieved a significant border security effect: year-to-date crossings remain low. This success, however, is undercut by a government impasse where lawmakers are deadlocked on funding, failing to provide the resources the enforcers deserve.",
